$R^{2}$ is defined as,
\begin{align*}
    R^{2} &= 1 - \dfrac{SSE}{SST} \\
    &= 1 - \frac{ ||Y - X\hat{\beta} ||^{2} }{ || Y - \bar{Y} ||^{2} } \\
\end{align*}
If $R^{2} = 1$, we must have $||Y - X\hat{\beta} ||^{2} = 0$. This means,
\begin{align*}
    0 &= ||Y - X\hat{\beta} ||^{2} \\
