    &= (Y_{1} - \hat{Y}_{i})^{2} + ... + (Y_{n} - \hat{Y}_{i})^{2}
\end{align*}
Since each term in the summation is squared, it must be positive. Thus, the only way the sum can equal 0 is if each individual term equals 0, which can only occur if $\hat{Y}_{i} = Y_{i}$ for all $i$.

